    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d869">

                <pb facs="0798" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/412A.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inform Clark negotiations in Europe promise successful results and bankers expect
                    to issue bonds as soon as formal authority for their execution is received from
                    Monrovia. Papers to be signed were mailed here by Falkner June 15. Bankers have
                    prepared form of provisional bonds and will execute them without delay when
                    authorizations requested have been received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
